meta {
  name: OIDC Callback
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/oidc/callback
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  state: {{oidc_state}}
  code: {{oidc_code}}
}

docs {
  This is the OIDC provider's redirect target, not an endpoint you call
  directly from Bruno — it's normally reached by the browser navigating
  away from the provider after login, carrying the state/code cookies
  set by GET /oidc/login. Calling it standalone will fail the
  oidc_state/oidc_nonce cookie checks.

  On success it either:
  - returns a JSON body (`model.LoginResponse`: token, refresh_token,
    user_id, username, role) directly, for a normal browser login, or
  - 302-redirects to the `cli_redirect_uri` supplied to GET /oidc/login
    with a one-time `?code=` for the CLI loopback flow, exchanged via
    POST /oidc/cli/exchange.
}
